            title: "Casino Hold'em",
            subtitle: 'Vs Dealer',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Casino Hold'em Poker is a casino table game introduced in 2001 by Stephen Au-Yeung. Based on Texas Hold'em, players compete against the house (not each other). Players make an ante bet, receive two hole cards, see a three-card flop, then decide to fold or place a play bet (2x ante). Best 5-card poker hand wins.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Casino Hold'em Poker was introduced by Stephen Au-Yeung in 2001. It was developed to capitalize on the enormous popularity of Texas Hold'em poker by creating a house-banked casino version.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
